Let $\mathrm{x}=$ number of $\mathrm{M}^{3+}$ ions
$\mathrm{y}=$ number of $\mathrm{M}^{2+}$ ions
Impure sample has $\mathrm{M}^{3+}$ ions. replacing $\mathrm{M}^{2+}$ ions.

\Rightarrow \mathrm{y}=0.96-\mathrm{x}

Total charge of metal atoms $=$ total charge of oxygen atoms.

\begin{aligned}
