By definition of volume strength
(a) 100 vol $\mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O}_2$ means

\begin{aligned}
& 1 \mathrm{~mL} \text { of } \mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O}_2 \equiv 100 \mathrm{~mL}^2 \mathrm{O}_2 \text { at STP } \\
& \therefore 2 \mathrm{~mL} \text { of } \mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O}_2 \equiv 2 \times 100=200 \mathrm{~mL} \text { of } \mathrm{O}_2 .
\end{aligned}

(b) $30 \mathrm{vol}$ of $\mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O}_2$ means

\begin{aligned}
& 1 \mathrm{~mL} \text { of } \mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O}_2 \equiv 30 \mathrm{~mL} \text { of } \mathrm{O}_2 \text { at STP. } \\
& \therefore 500 \mathrm{~mL} \text { of } \mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O}_2 \equiv 30 \times 500=15,000 \mathrm{~mL} \text { of } \mathrm{O}_2 \text {. }
\end{aligned}

(c) 10 vol of $\mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O}_2$ means
$1 \mathrm{~mL}$ of $\mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O}_2 \equiv 10 \mathrm{~mL}$ of $\mathrm{O}_2$ at STP.

\begin{aligned}
\therefore 1000 \mathrm{~mL}(1 \mathrm{~L}) \text { of } \mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O}_2 & \equiv 10 \times 1000 \text { of } \mathrm{O}_2 \\
& =10,000 \mathrm{~mL} \text { of } \mathrm{O}_2
\end{aligned}

(d) 20 vol of $\mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O}_2$ means

\begin{aligned}
& 1 \mathrm{~mL} \text { of } \mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O}_2 \equiv 20 \mathrm{~mL} \text { of } \mathrm{O}_2 \text { at STP. } \\
& \therefore 100 \mathrm{~mL} \text { of } \mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O}_2 \equiv 20 \times 100=2,000 \mathrm{~mL} \text { of } \mathrm{O}_2 \text {. }
\end{aligned}

Hence, $500 \mathrm{~mL}$ of $30 \mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O}_2$ gives highest volume of $\mathrm{O}_2$ at STP on complete decomposition.

